WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.002
Sparrow: Whew!

2
00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:07.005
It is so hot here!

3
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:10.408
Sparrow: I have been flying over this desert all day.

4
00:00:10.428 --> 00:00:13.370
Sparrow: I need to find a cool place to rest.

5
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:16.172
Sparrow: Look, there's a hole in the ground.

6
00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:17.633
I'll rest there.

7
00:00:29.703 --> 00:00:30.784
Who are you?

8
00:00:32.184 --> 00:00:33.924
Sparrow: Oh, I'm sorry.

9
00:00:34.425 --> 00:00:34.805
I am a sparrow.

10
00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:41.266
Sparrow: This desert is so dry and hot that I did not expect [n3@to see any animals living

11
00:00:41.346 --> 00:00:46.288
here! Mouse: I am a desert mouse, and there are a lot of animals here.

12
00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:48.928
Sparrow: Really?

13
00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.249
Mouse: Yes.

14
00:00:50.709 --> 00:00:54.310
The days are very hot and dry, but the nights are cold.

15
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.591
Mouse: So most desert animals do not move around during the day.

16
00:00:58.611 --> 00:01:02.012
Sparrow: But how do they endure so much heat?

17
00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:05.353
Sparrow: It is so hot that I am about to die!

18
00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:11.835
Mouse: Well, some desert animals use parts of their bodies to cool off.

19
00:01:11.855 --> 00:01:17.136
Mouse: For example, desert owls open their mouths [n3@wide and flutter their throats.

20
00:01:20.817 --> 00:01:24.298
The jackrabbit's ears are long and have many blood vessels.

21
00:01:24.458 --> 00:01:28.359
Mouse: The heat is released through the blood vessels in its long ears.

22
00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:31.420
Sparrow: Oh, that's interesting!

23
00:01:32.988 --> 00:01:37.609
Sparrow: Up north, I have seen other rabbits, and [n3@their ears are much shorter.

24
00:01:37.629 --> 00:01:41.770
Mouse: Yes, up north, they do not need long ears to survive.

25
00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:47.372
Mouse: All over the world, animals are suited to their different habitats.

26
00:01:47.452 --> 00:01:51.633
Mouse: For example, most desert animals are light-colored.

27
00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:55.374
Mouse: Their lighter colors keep them from getting really hot too.

28
00:01:55.394 --> 00:01:58.415
Sparrow: Then what about the darker animals?

29
00:01:58.435 --> 00:02:01.736
Sparrow: They would get much hotter than light-colored animals.

30
00:02:02.016 --> 00:02:04.669
Right? Mouse: You are right.

31
00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:08.791
Vultures are dark-colored, but they [n3@wet their legs with their urine.

32
00:02:08.811 --> 00:02:11.633
Mouse: The urine cools the blood in their legs.

33
00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:14.514
Mouse: The cooler blood goes back through their bodies.

34
00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.036
Sparrow: I see.

35
00:02:17.576 --> 00:02:19.157
They are really amazing!

36
00:02:19.177 --> 00:02:23.940
Sparrow: Then how do desert animals find water?

37
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.601
Sparrow: You do need water, don't you?

38
00:02:26.621 --> 00:02:28.302
Mouse: Of course!

39
00:02:28.742 --> 00:02:31.204
We desert creatures get water from plants.

40
00:02:33.004 --> 00:02:34.925
Mouse: The juicy cactus is a favorite!

41
00:02:35.265 --> 00:02:36.006
Have a piece!

42
00:02:36.026 --> 00:02:38.527
Sparrow: But won't I get stuck by the thorns?

43
00:02:38.547 --> 00:02:40.949
Mouse: Not really.

44
00:02:41.309 --> 00:02:42.950
Go ahead, just be careful.

45
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:47.813
Sparrow: Hmm, not bad!

46
00:02:50.054 --> 00:02:53.236
By the way, how do you stay cool in this desert?

47
00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:56.157
Mouse: I live in an underground den like this.

48
00:02:56.177 --> 00:02:58.979
Mouse: I close the opening when it is very hot.

49
00:02:59.419 --> 00:03:00.580
That keeps out the heat.

50
00:03:00.876 --> 00:03:03.398
Mouse: Then I can save the moisture from my breath.

51
00:03:03.418 --> 00:03:05.059
Sparrow: Wonderful!

52
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.122
Desert animals are really amazing.

53
00:03:09.142 --> 00:03:11.243
Sparrow: But I might not survive here.

54
00:03:11.263 --> 00:03:12.705
Mouse: That's true.

55
00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.986
The desert gets very little rain.

56
00:03:15.006 --> 00:03:18.709
Mouse: It gets less than 25 centimeters of rain a year!

57
00:03:18.729 --> 00:03:23.372
Mouse: So all the animals in the desert have special [n3@ways to help them survive.

58
00:03:23.392 --> 00:03:24.753
Mouse: But you have wings.

59
00:03:24.793 --> 00:03:28.316
Mouse: You can fly to a place where you will survive well.

60
00:03:29.964 --> 00:03:31.465
Sparrow: Yes, you are right!

61
00:03:31.946 --> 00:03:32.986
I have to leave now.

62
00:03:33.006 --> 00:03:35.969
Sparrow: Thank you for telling me about desert animals.

63
00:03:36.369 --> 00:03:38.611
Good-bye! Mouse: My pleasure!

64
00:03:38.871 --> 00:03:39.491
Good-bye!
